    <statement><p>Find an antiderivative <m>F(x)</m> of 
<m>f(x)=9 x - \sqrt{x}</m>.</p>
<p><m>F(x) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4.5x^{2}-0.666667x^{1.5}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f(x) = 9 x - x^{1/2}</m>, so <m>F(x)</m> must have the form 
<m>F(x) = \frac{9}{2} x^2 - \frac{2}{3} x^{3/2}</m>, or this plus any
constant value.



</solution>
